    "summary": "is_lib_type only checks for shadowing by a local interface (lookup_local_interface) plus may_be_ts_lib_type, which only sees module-level declarations and imports. A function-local `type Partial<T> = …` (or Pick/Omit/Required/Array) is never seen, so the name is treated as TypeScript's own.",
    "failure_scenario": "`function make(){ type Partial<T> = { wrapped: T }; return (p: { a?: Required<Partial<Data>> }) => null }`: the inner Partial goes through object_fields, then is_lib_type returns true, and the expansion becomes `{ x?: … }` instead of `{ wrapped: Data }`. The structural lane emits a wrong object where it should decline."
